      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the double-angle formula for sine and keep the multiplier.\n\nSet $x=\\frac{\\pi}{8}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sin x\\cos x &=\\sin(2x) \\\\ &=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute this exact value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)&=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
